ch Indauchen). The pepper's modern name is derived from the area where it is grown, the Province of Kampot, but its historic name uses the French term for Mainland Southeast Asia. Kampot peppers are similar to many other species of Piper."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-kampot-pepper"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kampot_pepper"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Cambodian cuisine","cuisine/cambodian-cuisine",[["Kampot pepper crab","dish/kampot-pepper-crab"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Crab","ingredient/crab"],["Fish sauce","ingredient/fish-sauce"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Palm sugar","ingredient/palm-sugar"],["Spring onions","ingredient/spring-onions"]]}]},"dish/kayabukiya-tavern":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/kayabukiya-tavern","n":"Kayabukiya Tavern","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Japanese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["The Kayabukiya Tavern was a traditional-style Japanese \"sake-house\" restaurant (izakaya) that was located in the city of Utsunomiya, north of Tokyo, Japan."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-kayabukiya-tavern"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kayabukiya_Tavern"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Just One Cookbook","ref":"site/justonecookbook-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"justonecookbook.com","note":"Namiko Chen's long-running blog and videos on Japanese home cooking.","url":"https://justonecookbook.com","suggested":true},{"name":"RecipeTin Japan","ref":"site/japan-recipetineats-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"japan.recipetineats.com","note":"Japanese home recipes from Yumiko, a Japan-born cook, sister site to RecipeTin Eats.","url":"https://japan.recipetineats.com/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Japanese cuisine","links":[["Benihana","dish/be